WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:03.021
The fifth case is one to the power infinity.

2
00:00:03.263 --> 00:00:06.178
Remember, the base only approaches one.

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.834
It is not the constant one.

4
00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:10.492
The example is one plus one over x,

5
00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.658
all raised to x.

6
00:00:11.908 --> 00:00:15.143
Call the expression y. The base is positive,

7
00:00:15.236 --> 00:00:18.459
so we can take its logarithm. ln y equals x

8
00:00:18.459 --> 00:00:20.465
multiplied by ln of one plus

9
00:00:20.465 --> 00:00:20.969
one over x.

10
00:00:21.275 --> 00:00:23.379
Set u equal to one divided by x.

11
00:00:23.451 --> 00:00:25.399
Then u approaches zero from the right.

12
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:28.101
ln y becomes ln of one plus u,

13
00:00:28.173 --> 00:00:28.919
divided by u.

14
00:00:29.197 --> 00:00:30.938
This is another standard limit,

15
00:00:30.946 --> 00:00:34.299
equal to one. Thus ln y tends to one.

16
00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:37.469
To return to y, apply the exponential function.

17
00:00:37.669 --> 00:00:39.538
The result is Euler's number e,

18
00:00:39.589 --> 00:00:42.093
approximately 2.718.

19
00:00:42.218 --> 00:00:44.002
It is this particular example that gives e.

20
00:00:44.138 --> 00:00:46.015
Not every expression of the form one

21
00:00:46.015 --> 00:00:47.906
to the power infinity has the same limit.

22
00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.084
Each expression needs its own calculation.
